\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.6}{\ignorespaces  Baseline and Topline performance across pretraining scales. The top row reports minimal-pair benchmark accuracy for Zorro and BLiMP. The bottom row reports grammaticality of generated utterances, using the ChildCG or GEC-based metric. Points show means across training runs (after averaging generation-based measures over generation seeds). Error bars show $\pm 1$ standard deviation across those runs. }}{104}{figure.5.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:topline}{{5.6}{104}{Baseline and Topline performance across pretraining scales. The top row reports minimal-pair benchmark accuracy for Zorro and BLiMP. The bottom row reports grammaticality of generated utterances, using the ChildCG or GEC-based metric. Points show means across training runs (after averaging generation-based measures over generation seeds). Error bars show $\pm 1$ standard deviation across those runs}{figure.5.6}{}}
\newlabel{fig:topline@cref}{{[figure][6][5]5.6}{[1][104][]104}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.7}{\ignorespaces  Benchmark performance across pretraining scales for each reward family. Rows show Zorro and BLiMP minimal-pair accuracy; columns show the four empirical reward families. Within each panel, the baseline and topline trajectories are repeated to make the reward trajectory directly comparable at each scale. Means are computed across training runs. Error bars show $\pm 1$ standard deviation across those runs; generation seeds do not provide independent model replications for fixed minimal-pair evaluation. }}{105}{figure.caption.103}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:benchmark_reward_scale}{{5.7}{105}{Benchmark performance across pretraining scales for each reward family. Rows show Zorro and BLiMP minimal-pair accuracy; columns show the four empirical reward families. Within each panel, the baseline and topline trajectories are repeated to make the reward trajectory directly comparable at each scale. Means are computed across training runs. Error bars show $\pm 1$ standard deviation across those runs; generation seeds do not provide independent model replications for fixed minimal-pair evaluation}{figure.caption.103}{}}
\newlabel{fig:benchmark_reward_scale@cref}{{[figure][7][5]5.7}{[1][104][]105}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.8}{\ignorespaces  Properties of generated utterances: Sentence length, pooled lexical entropy, function-word density, and rate of non-words. Points show means for each reward across training seeds, with error bars indicating $\pm 1$ standard deviation across these seeds. Within each panel, baseline and topline trajectories are repeated to make the reward trajectory directly comparable at each scale. }}{106}{figure.caption.104}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:covariates_reward_scale}{{5.8}{106}{Properties of generated utterances: Sentence length, pooled lexical entropy, function-word density, and rate of non-words. Points show means for each reward across training seeds, with error bars indicating $\pm 1$ standard deviation across these seeds. Within each panel, baseline and topline trajectories are repeated to make the reward trajectory directly comparable at each scale}{figure.caption.104}{}}
